      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While a good nap can help with short-term fatigue, trying to sleep off a prolonged feeling of heaviness or discomfort may not be the best idea. The sedatives in your sleep aids can also interfere with your sleep patterns and potentially worsen any underlying issues. If you're genuinely concerned about the heaviness in your arm, it's recommended to speak with a healthcare professional for guidance. Taking a longer nap of 4-5 hours might not be a safe solution, as it could affect your blood sugar levels, breathing, or even lead to more severe fatigue upon waking.",
